From f3393f8e01d473c0fcf750918e23d11047351e1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jawad Amin <jawadamin@google.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 10:34:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Write the compressed RoPE record in the byte-plane layout
 the gather reads

The compressor packed the 64 rotary channels as interleaved little-endian
BF16. `csa_gather` reads a different layout: it takes the high byte of
channel i from offset i, the low byte from offset 64 + i, and rebuilds the
value as (high << 8) | low. Every channel therefore decoded to an unrelated
number, and the sparse attention kernel attended against an arbitrary key.

The symptom was a finite but enormous value out of the first
compressed-attention layer, which the next RMSNorm turned into a nan that
spread to every later layer.

Pack the record as two byte planes to match the reader.

Measured on one host of a v6e slice with a normal latent. Before the change
the gathered RoPE reached 3.14e38 and held a nan where the written values
reached 2.55, and the sparse kernel returned 1.07e38. After it the gathered
RoPE returns 2.55 and the kernel returns 4.44.
---
 .../deepseek_v41/deepseek_v41_compressor.py     | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tpu_inference/layers/vllm/custom_ops/experimental/deepseek_v41/deepseek_v41_compressor.py b/tpu_inference/layers/vllm/custom_ops/experimental/deepseek_v41/deepseek_v41_compressor.py
index b1011a04..2ea41a6f 100644
--- a/tpu_inference/layers/vllm/custom_ops/experimental/deepseek_v41/deepseek_v41_compressor.py
+++ b/tpu_inference/layers/vllm/custom_ops/experimental/deepseek_v41/deepseek_v41_compressor.py
@@ -249,8 +249,14 @@ def build_kv_records(
 
     A latent stands for its whole group, so it rotates at the position of the
     group's first token. The NoPE record holds 448 FP8 E4M3 bytes then 7 E8M0
-    scale bytes, zero-padded to the record width. The RoPE record holds the 64
-    rotary channels in BF16.
+    scale bytes, zero-padded to the record width.
+
+    The RoPE record holds the 64 rotary channels in BF16 as two byte planes,
+    not as interleaved values. `csa_gather` reads the high byte of channel `i`
+    at offset `i` and the low byte at offset `64 + i`, and rebuilds the value
+    as `(high << 8) | low`. A record written as interleaved little-endian BF16
+    therefore decodes to a different number in every channel, and the sparse
+    kernel then sees an arbitrary key.
 
     This is a pure function of its arguments so a test can compare it against
     the CUDA kernel without a mesh.
@@ -263,8 +269,11 @@ def build_kv_records(
     nope_record = nope_record.at[:, :NOPE_CHANNELS].set(values)
     nope_record = nope_record.at[:, NOPE_CHANNELS:NOPE_CHANNELS +
                                  scales.shape[1]].set(scales)
-    rope_record = rotated[:, NOPE_CHANNELS:].astype(jnp.bfloat16).view(
-        jnp.uint8)
+    rope_bytes = rotated[:, NOPE_CHANNELS:].astype(jnp.bfloat16).view(
+        jnp.uint8).reshape(latent.shape[0], ROPE_CHANNELS, 2)
+    # The device is little-endian, so index 0 of a pair is the low byte.
+    rope_record = jnp.concatenate([rope_bytes[:, :, 1], rope_bytes[:, :, 0]],
+                                  axis=1)
     return nope_record, rope_record
 
 
